\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The spring again is here,
\par Life wakes from winter's gloom;
\par In field and forest far and near
\par Sweet opening flowerets bloom.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O mystery strange and sweet,
\par That life so dumbly bound,
\par Should rise, our thankful gaze to greet,
\par And break from underground.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The morn is fresh and bright,
\par The slow dark hours depart:
\par Let days unstained and pure delight
\par Bring sunshine to the heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord, touch our careless eyes;
\par New life, new ardour bring,
\par That we may read Thy mysteries,
\par The wonder of Thy spring.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

